values ('a3b4c5d6-7e8f-4a80-9b90-0d1e2f3a4b00', 'foundations-of-literacy-phonics-and-reading-science', 'Foundations of Literacy / Phonics & Reading Science', 'Frame reading as a learned language-literacy system grounded in oral language, print, cognition, instruction, and evidence. Build the linguistic foundation teachers need for phonics, spelling, vocabulary, and comprehension; teach how children notice and connect speech sounds, print, and letter-sound patterns; design systematic and advanced phonics for decoding, spelling, syllables, and morphology; and connect fluency, vocabulary, knowledge, and comprehension to structured literacy routines, assessment, intervention, multilingual learners, writing, and a capstone reading intervention plan.');

