ce, and teach the sound contrasts that underlie decoding and spelling."}, {"id": "80dbbf77-53e1-4f21-be06-5520de7c87d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language structure", "children": [{"id": "d84625ed-93e0-4b93-8b7d-9ca7b8d6670c", "type": "concept", "title": "Phonology"}, {"id": "9d0907bb-a766-4915-829a-3f0794ad9d1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Orthography"}, {"id": "e5fcd0ef-7bcb-4b1e-af8c-0252e1515f59", "type": "concept", "title": "Morphology"}, {"id": "9a10db39-593b-4aaf-8248-80c9c71d189c", "type": "concept", "title": "Syntax and semantics"}], "description": "Structured literacy depends on understanding how English works across sound, meaning, and sentence systems."}, {"id": "c39bdf68-a26b-4e41-9ae6-df6696a0cdbd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Oral language and literacy", "children": [{"id": "307fd6c0-be1f-4991-82fd-e6d9a8db7cf1", "type": "concept", "title": "Listening comprehension"}, {"id": "8b681584-3b76-42c6-8713-77be5571827c", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative language"}, {"id": "d8ae5896-ad99-4064-bb7e-bd8cd6d3b4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Dialogic talk"}, {"id": "601010d5-dfca-479b-938b-f36ac241ff04", "type": "concept", "title": "Academic language"}], "description": "Strong oral language supports vocabulary, comprehension, narrative skill, and later academic reading."}]}, {"id": "2d44936b-f9a8-4eb2-a3ed-d30c0dd9eceb", "type": "topic", "title": "Phonological and Phonemic Awareness", "description": "Teach how children notice, manipulate, and connect spoken sounds before and during reading development.", "children": [{"id": "65ba30c3-e787-4f66-a3de-f8acb4407154", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Phonological awareness continuum", "children": [{"id": "4e486177-b66c-4b61-a73a-9c3334b27b00", "type": "concept", "title": "Words and syllables"}, {"id": "42904480-fbff-4170-9664-07a1a5768359", "type": "concept", "title": "Onset-rime"}, {"id": "fea913ae-132b-4db5-ac0a-cd1367b3d952", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhyming"}, {"id": "32867d43-1cb1-4c2c-92f2-01b